      <p>
        Configuring operating systems to run on local time instead of UTC is considered an anti-pattern in infrastructure engineering. Database clusters using PostgreSQL, MySQL, or MongoDB, as well as Kubernetes container nodes, require UTC system clocks to execute scheduled cron tasks reliably without duplication during Daylight Saving Time switches.
      </p>
      <p>
